   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 929 of the laws of 1986 amending the tax law and other laws relating to the metropolitan transportation authority, in relation to extending certain provisions thereof applicable to the resolution of labor disputes",
    "basePrintNo": "S4738",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4738-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §45, Chap 929 of 1986",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4738\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 929 of the laws of 1986 amending the tax law\nand other laws relating to the metropolitan transportation authority,\nin relation to extending certain provisions thereof applicable to the\nresolution of labor disputes\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend to July 1, 2017, the provisions relating to compulsory\narbitration to resolve impasses in collective negotiations between the\nMetropolitan Transportation Authority (MTA), MTA New York City Transit\nor the MTA Bridges and Tunnels and employee organizations.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends section 45 of chapter 929 of the laws of\n1986, also amended by chapter 72 of the laws of 2013 to provide that\ncompulsory arbitration shall be extended until July 1, 2017.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that this act shall take effect\nimmediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe current provisions of Chapter 929 of the Laws of 1986 relating to\ncompulsory arbitration to resolve impasses in collective negotiations\nbetween an MTA public employer and a public employee organization\ncertified or recognized to represent employees of such MTA public\nemployer will expire on July 1, 2015. Compulsory arbitration has\nallowed the people of New York to enjoy uninterrupted service. All\nevaluations of the effects of this law have been positive and have\nadvocated the continuation of this process. This bill extends the time\nperiod until July 1, 2017 for compulsory arbitration.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
